=== SURVEY ===
Web source globalShortcuts.tsx is a headless registry populator (`return null`): it builds a
`ShortcutDefinition[]` via `useTranslation` + `useShortcut(defs)` so the cheat-sheet has one
source of truth. Three families (verbatim):
  • Actions (4 universals): Ctrl+K / "/" → Open command palette; ? → Show keyboard shortcuts;
    Esc → Close modal / cancel.
  • Navigation (press g then…) (14 from GOTO_SHORTCUTS): g d Dashboard, g v Vehicles, g c
    Charging, g r Drives, g t Trips, g b Battery & Energy, g a Analytics, g e Efficiency,
    g s Settings, g n Notifications, g l Live Signals, g o Automations, g x Commands, g i Climate.
  • Commands (3 commandRegistry entries with `shortcut`): T Open theme picker, ? Show keyboard
    shortcuts, E Edit dashboard layout.
Data sources (P1/S8): useTranslation, useShortcut. Shared components: none. Charts/maps: none.
i18n keys: shortcuts.groups.{actions,navigation,commands}, shortcuts.{openPalette,openPaletteAlt,
openShortcuts,close,goto}, plus the command labelKeys (palette.cmd.*) and goto target labels.
Existing native: no `GlobalShortcuts`/`ShortcutKeyToken`/`GlobalShortcutsCatalog` symbols (no
collision). Existing shared `TSKeyboardShortcutsModal`/`TSCode` reused for the keycap idiom.
Canonical surface pattern studied: AchievementBadge (Adapter/Model/Views/States/Previews/strings/
Tests/ModelTests).

=== REASONING ===
- The web component renders nothing; the prompt requires a production-polished native surface
  reproducing its DATA, composition, states, and i18n. Chosen: present the same registry as the
  keyboard-shortcuts reference (the grouping the web cheat-sheet performs at read time), modelled
  as a pure projection so it is fully unit-testable.
- Architecture mirrors the canonical AchievementBadge leaf: pure Adapter (catalog = verbatim port
  of the web `defs`, key-token model, grouping, a11y) + Model (P1/S8 state-holder seam, P1/S11
  telemetry, P1/S10 i18n facade, connection axis, projection, @Observable model, canonical +
  in-memory sources) + View/Views/States + Previews + strings + Tests/ModelTests.
- States rendered: loading (skeleton sections), empty (no registered shortcuts), error (retry),
  data (grouped cheat-sheet), and the orthogonal connection axis stale/offline (freshness chip +
  one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition).
- Rejected: porting Tailwind classes (used P1/S9 tokens instead); a flat ungrouped list (the web
  groups by the `group` field — reproduced); direct HTTP in the view (bound via the source seam).
- Build inclusion (necessary infra, documented): TeslaSync/misc-surfaces was NOT yet a source dir
  in project.yml nor in .swiftlint.yml `included`. Both were wired (mirroring feature-views /
  dashboard-widgets) so the gate actually COMPILES + LINTS this surface — without it the gate
  would pass vacuously over zero of my files (that would itself be red-as-green). Idempotent and
  mergeable with sibling misc-surfaces prompts (0001 TourLauncher, 0003 selectedVehicle).

